{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1nPNEgCKnqtcJtkeGG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Build it, but ship it as a randomized experiment rather than a full launch. Don't spend the three weeks on more research first.**\n\n**Why building is justified**\n- The email evidence is strong. It was a randomized trial, so the reminder caused the drop. With about 400 patients per arm, a 13-point fall (31% to 18%) has a 95% confidence interval of roughly ±6 points, so it's very unlikely to be noise.\n- The control group's late rate (31%) matches the overall rate in pharmacy records. That suggests email opt-ins aren't unusually punctual, which makes the result more believable for everyone.\n- The cost is small and easy to undo: two engineers for three weeks. More research would likely take about as long as building.\n\n**What the trial doesn't tell you**\n- **Channel:** a push notification isn't an email. Push is quicker to notice but easier to ignore or switch off. The effect could be bigger or smaller.\n- **Reach:** the result only helps patients who have the app with push turned on. If that's 15% of repeat patients, the overall impact is small, however well push works.\n- **Overlap:** if those patients already get the email reminder (or will once it's rolled out), the real question is what push adds on top of email, and that could be close to nothing.\n\n**Two quick checks before coding (about a day of data work)**\n1. What share of repeat-prescription patients have push turned on, and how many of them are also email opt-ins?\n2. Has the email reminder been rolled out to everyone yet? If not, do that first. It's proven and probably cheaper.\n\n**How to build it**\n- Randomly hold out a group of push-enabled patients who get no push reminder. Include one arm that gets both email and push.\n- Measure late collection from pharmacy records, not app opens. Also track how many people turn off notifications.\n- Decide in advance what improvement justifies rolling out to everyone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3193,"cache_read_input_tokens":5027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3193},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2678e259-e7e9-413d-b3ce-7a05a0d64983","uuid":"f0cbf8e3-ccc3-4f8b-abe8-19d23c56610a","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:16:46.732Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1nPA5dw4hdcWobwesy"}
